{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012QJMg9Ja42ibSZxZYx2b6g","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Codebase Exploration Report\n\n### 1. Project Structure Overview\n\nThis is a **Next.js 16.1.6** project with TypeScript, using the **App Router** pattern. The structure is:\n\n```\n/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/\n├── src/\n│   ├── app/\n│   │   ├── [locale]/\n│   │   │   ├── layout.tsx          (Root layout with i18n setup)\n│   │   │   └── page.tsx            (Home page)\n│   │   ├── api/\n│   │   │   └── health/\n│   │   │       └── route.ts        (Health check endpoint)\n│   │   ├── globals.css             (Tailwind + theme CSS)\n│   │   └── favicon.ico\n│   ├── components/\n│   │   └── language-switcher.tsx   (i18n language switcher)\n│   ├── lib/\n│   │   ├── supabase.ts            (Supabase client init)\n│   │   └── utils.ts               (cn() utility - clsx + tailwind-merge)\n│   ├── i18n/\n│   │   ├── config.ts              (Locale config: EN, ES)\n│   │   ├── routing.ts             (next-intl routing setup)\n│   │   └── request.ts             (i18n server config)\n│   └── middleware.ts              (next-intl middleware)\n├── messages/\n│   ├── en.json                    (English translations)\n│   └── es.json                    (Spanish translations)\n├── package.json\n├── next.config.ts\n├── tsconfig.json\n├── postcss.config.mjs\n├── components.json                (shadcn config)\n└── .env.local\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Existing Layout Files\n\n**Root Layout: `/src/app/[locale]/layout.tsx`**\n- Locale-based routing with dynamic `[locale]` segment\n- Uses Google Fonts (Geist Sans & Mono)\n- Implements `NextIntlClientProvider` for client-side translation\n- Generates static params for both EN and ES locales\n- Handles dynamic metadata generation based on locale\n\n**Home Page: `/src/app/[locale]/page.tsx`**\n- Uses `useTranslations()` hook for server-side translation keys\n- Includes a `LanguageSwitcher` component positioned top-right\n- Contains placeholder content (Next.js template)\n- Implements rich text translations with links\n\n---\n\n### 3. Internationalization (i18n) Setup\n\n**Translation System: `next-intl` v4.8.2**\n\n**Configuration Files:**\n- `/src/i18n/config.ts` - Defines supported locales: `['es', 'en']` (Spanish default)\n- `/src/i18n/routing.ts` - Defines routing rules using `defineRouting()`\n- `/src/i18n/request.ts` - Server-side request config that imports JSON messages dynamically\n\n**Message Files:**\n- `/messages/en.json` - English translations with keys:\n  - `common.{language, spanish, english}`\n  - `home.{title, description, templates, learning, deployNow, documentation}`\n  - `metadata.{title, description}`\n\n- `/messages/es.json` - Spanish translations (same structure)\n\n**Middleware:**\n- `/src/middleware.ts` - Uses `next-intl/middleware` to handle locale prefix routing\n- Matcher configuration to include all routes except API, _next, _vercel, and static files\n\n**Language Switcher Component:**\n- Located at `/src/components/language-switcher.tsx`\n- Client component that switches locales without page reload\n- Displays buttons for each supported locale\n- Current locale highlighted with foreground/background colors\n\n---\n\n### 4. UI Components & Styling\n\n**Styling Approach: Tailwind CSS v4 + CSS Variables**\n\n**Global CSS: `/src/app/globals.css`**\n- Uses Tailwind v4 with `@import \"tailwindcss\"` and `@import \"tw-animate-css\"`\n- Custom CSS variables for theming (oklch color format)\n- Theme variables defined for:\n  - Base colors: background, foreground, primary, secondary, destructive, etc.\n  - Sidebar colors and states\n  - Chart colors (5 variants)\n  - Border radius variants (sm, md, lg, xl, 2xl, 3xl, 4xl)\n- **Dark mode support** with `.dark` class selector\n- Base layer rules for border colors and outline rings\n\n**shadcn Configuration: `/components.json`**\n- UI component library setup with shadcn/ui\n- Style: \"new-york\", tsx: true, RSC: true\n- Icon library: lucide-react\n- Component aliases configured for organized imports\n\n**Utility Functions:**\n- `/src/lib/utils.ts` - Exports `cn()` function combining:\n  - `clsx()` for conditional classnames\n  - `tailwind-merge()` for safe Tailwind class merging\n\n**Installed UI/Styling Dependencies:**\n- `tailwindcss@4` (latest)\n- `@tailwindcss/postcss@4`\n- `lucide-react@0.563.0` (icons)\n- `radix-ui@1.4.3` (headless UI primitives)\n- `class-variance-authority@0.7.1` (component variants)\n- `clsx@2.1.1` (classname utilities)\n- `tailwind-merge@3.4.0` (smart Tailwind class merging)\n\n---\n\n### 5. Authentication Setup\n\n**Supabase Integration:**\n- Supabase JS client v2.93.3 installed\n- Client initialization at `/src/lib/supabase.ts`:\n  - Uses `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` env vars\n  - Throws error if env vars are missing\n  - Currently configured with local Supabase emulator defaults\n\n**Health Check Endpoint: `/src/app/api/health/route.ts`**\n- GET endpoint at `/api/health`\n- Attempts to verify Supabase connection\n- Returns JSON with status, supabase connection state, and timestamp\n- Error handling for connection failures\n\n**Environment Variables:**\n- `.env.local` contains local development Supabase credentials (emulator)\n- `.env.example` provides template for production setup\n- Public keys are prefixed with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` for client-side access\n\n---\n\n### 6. Key Project Metadata\n\n**Main Dependencies:**\n- Next.js 16.1.6 (latest)\n- React 19.2.3\n- TypeScript 5\n- next-intl 4.8.2\n- Supabase client 2.93.3\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Multi-locale routing (ES/EN)\n- Server-side translations with client fallback\n- Supabase backend integration\n- Modern Tailwind CSS v4 setup\n- Component library ready (shadcn aliases configured)\n- Dark mode support\n- TypeScript with path aliases (`@/*` → `./src/*`)\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nThe project is a well-structured Next.js application with:\n1. **Locale-aware routing** using next-intl with ES/EN support\n2. **Comprehensive styling** using Tailwind v4 with CSS variables and dark mode\n3. **Backend integration** with Supabase (initialized but minimal usage)\n4. **UI framework ready** with shadcn/ui component library aliases\n5. **Type-safe development** with TypeScript and proper path aliases\n6. **Minimal starter content** - placeholder Next.js home page waiting for real content\n\nThe app is production-ready from an infrastructure perspective, with only content/features remaining to be developed."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aed19aa (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31e11c92-fa49-434c-8a96-7f8081101436","uuid":"054d00b9-23e4-4a22-8e58-9b77b6ef63c9","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the codebase to understand:\n1. The current project structure (Next.js app router setup)\n2. Existing layout files\n3. Internationalization setup (i18n, translations)\n4. Any existing UI components or styling (Tailwind, etc.)\n5. Authentication setup if any\n\nFocus on:\n- src/app directory structure\n- Any existing components\n- Translation files and i18n configuration\n- Styling approach (Tailwind config, CSS files)","agentId":"aed19aa","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Codebase Exploration Report\n\n### 1. Project Structure Overview\n\nThis is a **Next.js 16.1.6** project with TypeScript, using the **App Router** pattern. The structure is:\n\n```\n/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/\n├── src/\n│   ├── app/\n│   │   ├── [locale]/\n│   │   │   ├── layout.tsx          (Root layout with i18n setup)\n│   │   │   └── page.tsx            (Home page)\n│   │   ├── api/\n│   │   │   └── health/\n│   │   │       └── route.ts       