lwind class merging)\n\n---\n\n### 5. Authentication Setup\n\n**Supabase Integration:**\n- Supabase JS client v2.93.3 installed\n- Client initialization at `/src/lib/supabase.ts`:\n  - Uses `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` env vars\n  - Throws error if env vars are missing\n  - Currently configured with local Supabase emulator defaults\n\n**Health Check Endpoint: `/src/app/api/health/route.ts`**\n- GET endpoint at `/api/health`\n- Attempts to verify Supabase connection\n- Returns JSON with status, supabase connection state, and timestamp\n- Error handling for connection failures\n\n**Environment Variables:**\n- `.env.local` contains local development Supabase credentials (emulator)\n- `.env.example` provides template for production setup\n- Public keys are prefixed with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` for client-side access\n\n---\n\n### 6. Key Project Metadata\n\n**Main Dependencies:**\n- Next.js 16.1.6 (latest)\n- React 19.2.3\n- TypeScript 5\n- next-intl 4.8.2\n- Supabase client 2.93.3\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Multi-locale routing (ES/EN)\n- Server-side translations with client fallback\n- Supabase backend integration\n- Modern Tailwind CSS v4 setup\n- Component library ready (shadcn aliases configured)\n- Dark mode support\n- TypeScript with path aliases (`@/*` → `./src/*`)\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nThe project is a well-structured Next.js application with:\n1. **Locale-aware routing** using next-intl with ES/EN support\n2. **Comprehensive styling** using Tailwind v4 with CSS variables and dark mode\n3. **Backend integration** with Supabase (initialized but minimal usage)\n4. **UI framework ready** with shadcn/ui component library aliases\n5. **Type-safe development** with TypeScript and proper path aliases\n6. **Minimal starter content** - placeholder Next.js home page waiting for real content\n\nThe app is production-ready from an infrastructure perspective, with only content/features remaining to be developed."}],"totalDurationMs":40927,"totalToken